# PR workflow

- Before every commit, run `make mr` and fix failures.
- One action = one commit. Do not batch unrelated changes.
- After any change meant for review, commit and push to the open PR immediately.
- If the current branch is `main`, create a new branch first with a short kebab-case name (one or two words, e.g. `pypi`, `fix-cli`).
- Keep the PR description current: set it on create, and update it after every commit so it matches the full PR diff.
- Do not leave reviewable work uncommitted on a PR branch.
